    "narrative": "Our offensive outlook for today is headlined by the singular active start for **Brice Turang**, who carries a 50.35 score into his matchup against Yamamoto. While an xERA of 3.40 against an elite arm like Yamamoto tempers the enthusiasm, **Brice Turang**\u2019s placement in the two-hole provides significant value, offering the high-leverage opportunities needed to manufacture runs. We are heavily prioritizing his sprint speed potential here, despite a 4% drag on his projection due to the high probability of the opposition prioritizing holding runners on base. Given that **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Josh Naylor** are all sidelined by team off-days, our offensive engine is essentially running on a single cylinder, making the efficiency of **Brice Turang** critical for our 5x5 Roto standing today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the starting threshold with a 37.36 score. While his recent performance metrics suggest he is locked in, the combination of a difficult 3.30 xERA matchup against Rasmussen and a suppressive park environment pushed him below our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. We are opting to bench **Travis Bazzana** rather than risk eroding our batting average and game-cap efficiency against a high-tier arm. Elsewhere, the absence of **James Wood**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young** leaves us with no further personnel to deploy. We are effectively in a preservation posture, keeping our bench assets fresh and avoiding the floor of sub-40 projected performers until the schedule opens up tomorrow.",
